{
 "lines": [
  {
   "id": "l0",
   "start": 0.1,
   "end": 5.817,
   "text": "Five thousand dollars on a credit card. Eight thousand, eight hundred eighty seven in interest."
  },
  {
   "id": "l1",
   "start": 6.067,
   "end": 9.177,
   "text": "That's if you only pay the minimum, at twenty four percent."
  },
  {
   "id": "l2",
   "start": 9.377,
   "end": 11.297,
   "text": "And it takes nineteen and a half years."
  },
  {
   "id": "l3",
   "start": 11.847,
   "end": 14.597,
   "text": "Now pay a fixed two hundred fifty a month instead."
  },
  {
   "id": "l4",
   "start": 14.797,
   "end": 18.287,
   "text": "Twenty six months. Fourteen hundred forty nine in interest."
  },
  {
   "id": "l5",
   "start": 18.587,
   "end": 22.043,
   "text": "You just kept seven thousand, four hundred thirty eight dollars."
  },
  {
   "id": "l6",
   "start": 22.443,
   "end": 25.473,
   "text": "Never pay the minimum. Pick a fixed number, and stick to it."
  },
  {
   "id": "l7",
   "start": 25.773,
   "end": 29.003,
   "text": "Follow for part two: how to drop that rate to zero."
  }
 ],
